HPLIP 3.25.2
https://sourceforge.net/projects/hplip/files/hplip/3.25.2/hplip-3.25.2.tar.gz

ppd/hplip/*.ppd.gz are copied unchanged from ppd/hpcups/ in the tarball.
They are HP's files and keep HP's headers. Only the PPDs the package can
serve are vendored (see the rules at the top of scripts/gen-ppds.py);
ppd/hplip/manifest.tsv lists them and ppd/hplip/excluded.tsv lists the
rest with the reason each was left out.

To refresh after an HPLIP upgrade, unpack the tarball and run:

    scripts/gen-ppds.py select --hplip <path to hplip-X.Y.Z>

That rewrites the vendored files, both manifests and
docs/supported-printers.md.

The installed PPDs are made at build time by `scripts/gen-ppds.py build`.
Changes made to each PPD on the way:
- *cupsFilter points at /Library/Printers/hpcups-macos/filter/hpcups.
- *NickName becomes "<model name>, hpcups-macos" and *ShortNickName is
  rewritten to fit the 31 character limit.
- Duplicate *PageSize, *PageRegion, *PaperDimension and *ImageableArea
  choices are dropped, and *UIConstraints that name a paper size the PPD
  does not offer are dropped. cupstestppd rejects both.
*1284DeviceID, *Product and *ModelName are left alone so macOS can match
a plugged-in printer to its PPD.
